{
  "_note": "LOS HITOS, as data. What each landmark type LOOKS like, keyed by LandmarkType — the same `switch` the renderer used to carry as 26 branches of raw Canvas calls. The world says WHERE a landmark stands (churchill/world/content.py -> manifest.landmarks); this says what is drawn there, in the same spirit as feriaAssets.json and vehicles.json.",

  "version": 1,

  "_geometry": "Plain PIXEL offsets from the landmark's anchor, +y down — the frame the art was already written in (`ctx.fillRect(x - 16, y - 8, 32, 18)` becomes `x: -16, y: -8, w: 32, h: 18`). Parts are drawn in order, so later ones sit on top.",

  "_shapes": "The finite vocabulary in src/render/c2d/shapes.js, shared with the vehicle catalog: rect, roundRect, poly, fan, ellipse, disc, stripes, stroke, strokeRect, text, label, areaLabel, repeat, grid. Data composes these and never invents one.",

  "_scenes": "Three types are NOT here and must not be moved: `lighthouse`, `park` (when marine) and `stadium` call drawFaroScene / drawMarinePark / drawStadium. Those are SCENES, not art — the faro sweeps a beam on the clock, the estadio clips grass and stands to a footprint the build emitted, the marine park fills a multi-ring even-odd residual. §12's own list says a Canvas command stream with unrestricted operations does not become JSON; these are that.",

  "landmarks": {
